{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command '$script = @'\"'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport re,difflib\nfiles={'docs/requirements/low-level-requirements.toml':{\n'LLR-061':'detail = \\\"\\\"\\\"The worker accepts an explicit work-item assignment with train and worktree context; its prompt carries the assigned row, specification reference, predecessor context, train diff and rework finding, excludes the generated status surface, and retains collision-safe assignment evidence. A one-item assignment names the branch the claim cut and defaults the session tag to that branch. Empty, malformed or multi-item assignments refuse before a session starts; the multi-row prompt block and retired track machinery do not participate. A worker edits neither root status, another branch’s claim, the root log nor generated artifacts, and its result is committed trailer evidence.\\\"\\\"\\\"',\n'LLR-144':'detail = \\\"\\\"\\\"A partial close refuses a claim other than one spec before report or state change, commits the lane work as-is, moves the one spec to terminal partial state, and writes one immutable report naming outcome, reason, commit range and keep/discard split. The report is immutable and unique; a second close refuses rather than overwriting it, and a refusal restores the one report it created. The terminal move prevents re-claiming. Quarantine reverts product paths to the merge base, preserves the failing diff as a bar-inert patch, reads each rename as a record so it cannot revert the wrong path, checks every version-control result, and restores rather than reports if a revert fails. Each outcome leaves the branch finished and every lane reaches a merge.\\\"\\\"\\\"',\n'LLR-149':'detail = \\\"\\\"\\\"The admission decision applies the ruled kind-by-approval table. A human-held attestation or gate row surfaces even under keep-nondependent, which governs other lanes rather than approval. An exclusive frontier row stops new admission until every lane returns; the first spine row then admits alone ahead of ordinary work and remaining spine rows wait for later exclusive turns. Held rows drain and surface, and at a delegated tier dispatch one at a time, exclusive. The lane count resolves the command-line value, then the environment value, then the declared setting, then one; an absent, malformed or below-one value falls to serial. The empty-frontier census names unverified in-scope requirements, orphan rows and draft needs mechanically and hands them to the intake mint rather than minting in a lane.\\\"\\\"\\\"',\n'LLR-150':'detail = \\\"\\\"\\\"One lane ensures its worktree, forwards the launch session dials to its worker, hands that worker one item, and runs the station refresh as the lane’s own overlapping subprocess so lane bars do not queue at admission. It reports outcomes but decides none: the assigned specification leaving the claim directory and the exit code are the protocol. A parked resume refuses an assignment other than one item before mutation or launch.\\\"\\\"\\\"',\n'LLR-151':'detail = \\\"\\\"\\\"The claim requires the dispatch lock, taken at one site after the refusal ladder so the lock does not create a refusal of its own. A hand claim on an idle station works; a hand claim during live lanes is unrepresentable; a lock-held caller proceeds without taking it again. One claim commit moves one queued specification and cuts its branch. Empty or multi-item input refuses before lock, move, commit, branch or worktree. Historical multi-item claim commits remain readable and are neither split nor re-claimed; each branch refresh remains independently restricted.\\\"\\\"\\\"',\n'LLR-152':'detail = \\\"\\\"\\\"The adjudication kind is exclusive at rank one. Its lane runs no product bar because its outputs are status cells and the work registry; its refresh still incorporates trunk, runs the trunk step, and commits a verified no-bar attestation. A lane whose one claimed row is any other kind, or whose frontmatter is unreadable, runs the bar. The declared bar key states verification strictness without affecting scheduling; the refresh forwards that one row’s key to the gate check, absent keys forward none, and malformed values refuse before refresh.\\\"\\\"\\\"',\n'LLR-161':'detail = \\\"\\\"\\\"The close writes its report first, refuses when one already exists, and restores the one report it created on refusal while leaving claim and terminal state unchanged. A terminal specification without a report refuses loudly. Every partial or cancelled close earns one disposition: a re-sweep mints none, a genuinely second close is a second report and therefore a second row, and a disposition cannot mint one for itself. A complete close is spot-checked at the declared rate. Continuing partial work drafts an explicitly linked successor without reopening a terminal row. A disposition that owes a successor drafts one or adopts an already-filed one that supersedes the disposed row.\\\"\\\"\\\"',\n'LLR-207':'detail = \\\"\\\"\\\"The verdict record derives one identity for a work tree, verifies refresh and review attestations against their own trees and parents, and reads unavailable repository answers fail-closed. A mechanical close is disposable only when it moves exactly one row under the work registry and its scalar subject matches that row. Cardinality refuses empty and multi-row shapes; one deletion implies one source branch. A refused shape declines to peel toward more review. The identity walk traverses only identity-preserving committed evidence, while the destructive reset path removes only a verified refresh at the tip. Review evidence remains bound to the governing identity, declared phase span and admissible scope.\\\"\\\"\\\"'},\n'docs/test/test-cases.toml':{\n'TC-061':'method = \\\"\\\"\\\"Drive the worker loop against a fake provider in throwaway repositories from explicit work-item and train assignments and from a work-item assignment alone. The prompt carries the assigned row, specification reference, predecessor context and trailer protocol, excludes generated status, and retains the declared close and context behavior. An empty, malformed, repeated or multi-item assignment refuses before provider launch; the one-row prompt names its one assignment. A committed completion trailer while the specification remains open reads built but not done. The result, relaunch, blocked, budget, review, concurrent-worker, managed-review and preflight refusal behaviors retain their stated assertions.\\\"\\\"\\\"',\n'TC-138':'method = \\\"\\\"\\\"Run the handback suite: a partial close refuses an empty or multi-spec claim before report or state change; a one-spec close moves the terminal specification, writes its immutable report, leaves the branch finished, is clean under the real trajectory check, refuses a second close without residue, and is loud when a terminal specification has no report. The close does not write a block reference, preserves an existing deliverable, and refuses a branch without a trunk claim. Quarantine reverts product paths, preserves the failing patch, handles a rename record-wise, leaves handback bookkeeping alone, refuses a non-lane red, and restores rather than reports after failed revert.\\\"\\\"\\\"',\n'TC-143':'method = \\\"\\\"\\\"Run dispatch admission: an exclusive row plus a busy lane waits while a frontier without one fills lanes; when lanes return, the first spine row admits alone ahead of ordinary work. The approval table surfaces held rows, preserves non-dependent work only where declared, and dispatches autonomous held rows exclusively. The lane-count ladder resolves command line, environment, declared setting and serial fallback for absent, malformed and below-one values. The gap census names unverified requirements, orphan rows and draft needs mechanically and is empty on a registry-less repository; classification agrees at every quarantine.\\\"\\\"\\\"',\n'TC-144':'method = \\\"\\\"\\\"Run the dispatch loop on real repositories: each spine claim moves one item and its worker receives that item; the next waits for the exclusive lane’s return. A one-item parked lane resumes under the barrier; empty or multi-item assignment refuses before mutation or launch. A needs-human worker hands back, lane refresh runs as its own subprocess, a red refresh quarantines and stops the run, an attended gate drains and exits with its approvals banner, and the empty-frontier census hands gaps to intake. Pause, dirty-trunk, stall and crash-resume retain their serial-loop contracts.\\\"\\\"\\\"',\n'TC-145':'method = \\\"\\\"\\\"Run the claim suite: a spine claim succeeds on an idle station; a hand claim while another holder owns the dispatch lock refuses naming the lock and leaves the queue untouched, while a lock-held caller proceeds. One item claims in one bookkeeping commit; empty and multi-item input refuse with no partial claim; historical multi-item records are neither re-claimed nor split. The abandoned-claim re-cut, relink, minted-id, bookkeeping audit and scratch-worktree isolation arms retain their stated assertions, including preservation and naming of concurrent drift and cleanup after success, refusal or crash.\\\"\\\"\\\"',\n'TC-146':'method = \\\"\\\"\\\"Run adjudication cases: the kind is exclusive at rank one; an adjudication-only lane runs no product bar yet records a verified no-bar attestation, while a lane whose one row is any other kind runs the bar. A declared bar reaches the gate check as its gate under the recording stub, an undeclared bar passes no gate, and a malformed value refuses the refresh naming it.\\\"\\\"\\\"',\n'TC-154':'method = \\\"\\\"\\\"Run loop ordering: an adjudication row admits ahead of a ready spine work item while the ruled rank table is unchanged; the partition is stable and cannot move work past a human-held stop; the completion and census grammar assertions retain their stated cases.\\\"\\\"\\\"',\n'TC-156':'method = \\\"\\\"\\\"Run handback over real worktrees: a partial close is clean under the real trajectory check, a terminal specification without a report is loud, a second close refuses without residue, an injected refusal after the one report restores it while leaving claim and terminal state unchanged, and disposition, re-sweep, drafting and adoption retain their stated assertions.\\\"\\\"\\\"',\n'TC-205':'method = \\\"\\\"\\\"Drive verdict identity, evidence, phase, scope and attestation behavior beside their refusal cases. A mechanical close is admitted only for one moved row under the work registry with its scalar subject; empty and multi-row shapes do not peel and therefore fail toward more review. A real close and the verifier agree on that identity, while malformed subjects, outside paths, injected or destroyed records, invalid evidence, and unavailable repository answers retain their stated refusals.\\\"\\\"\\\"'}}\nprint('*** Begin Patch')\nfor fn,rows in files.items():\n p=Path(fn);o=p.read_text();n=o\n for ident,val in rows.items():\n  pat=r'(\\\\['+('design' if 'LLR' in ident else 'test')+r'\\\\.'+ident+r'\\\\][\\\\s\\\\S]*?\\\\n)(detail|method) = .*?(?=\\\\n(?:rationale|test_refs|tier) =)'\n  n,c=re.subn(pat,lambda m:m.group(1)+val,n,count=1)\n  if c\"'!=1:raise SystemExit(ident)\n print('\"'*** Update File: '+str(p.resolve()))\n for x in difflib.unified_diff(o.splitlines(),n.splitlines(),n=1,lineterm=''):\n  if x.startswith(('---','+++')):continue\n  print('@@' if x.startswith('@@') else x)\nprint('*** End Patch')\n'@\n& 'C:/Projects/ai-template/.venv/Scripts/python.exe' -c \"'$script'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
