 worktree context. Its prompt names that one row with its identifier, title, specification reference and predecessor context; an empty, malformed or multi-item assignment refuses before a session starts, and the multi-row prompt block retires. The assignment is the branch the claim cut, the session tag defaults to the branch name, the prompt excludes the generated status surface, and the result channel is committed trailer evidence.\"\r\n+detail = \"\"\"The worker accepts an explicit work-item assignment with train and worktree context; its prompt carries the assigned row, specification reference, predecessor context, train diff and rework finding, excludes the generated status surface, and retains collision-safe assignment evidence. A one-item assignment names the branch the claim cut and defaults the session tag to that branch. Empty, malformed or multi-item assignments refuse before a session starts; the multi-row prompt block and retired track machinery do not participate. A worker edits neither root status, another branch�s claim, the root log nor generated artifacts, and its result is committed trailer evidence.\"\"\"\r\n test_refs = \"(see TC-061)\"\r\n@@\r\n code_symbol = \"close_partial/quarantine/report_path/render_report/_restore/diff_records\"\r\n-detail = \"\"\"A partial close refuses a claim other than one spec before any report or state change. It moves that one spec to the terminal partial state and writes one immutable per-close report naming the outcome, reason, commit range and keep/discard split. A second close refuses rather than overwriting the report, and a refusal restores the one report it created while leaving the claim and terminal state unchanged. The quarantine outcome retains its existing red-bar recovery contract.\"\"\"\r\n+detail = \"\"\"A partial close refuses a claim other than one spec before report or state change, commits the lane work as-is, moves the one spec to terminal partial state, and writes one immutable report naming outcome, reason, commit range and keep/discard split. The report is immutable and unique; a second close refuses rather than overwriting it, and a refusal restores the one report it created. The terminal move prevents re-claiming. Quarantine reverts product paths to the merge base, preserves the failing diff as a bar-inert patch, reads each rename as a record so it cannot revert the wrong path, checks every version-control result, and restores rather than reports if a revert fails. Each outcome leaves the branch finished and every lane reaches a merge.\"\"\"\r\n rationale = \"\"\"Making the outcome the directory leaves no fourth answer and no state file that could hold one; partial work lands in trunk where a future WI can find it instead of on a branch nobody will look at.\"\"\"\r\n@@\r\n code_symbol = \"_kind_action/_admission/_lane_count/gap_census\"\r\n-detail = \"\"\"The admission decision applies the ruled kind-by-approval table. A human-held attestation or gate row surfaces even under keep-nondependent, which governs other lanes rather than approval; an exclusive frontier row stops new admission until every lane returns, then the first spine row admits alone ahead of ordinary work and remaining spine rows wait for later exclusive turns. Held attestation and gate rows drain and surface, and keep-nondependent never releases their hold; at a delegated tier they dispatch one at a time, exclusive. The lane-count ladder and empty-frontier gap census retain their existing contracts.\"\"\"\r\n+detail = \"\"\"The admission decision applies the ruled kind-by-approval table. A human-held attestation or gate row surfaces even under keep-nondependent, which governs other lanes rather than approval. An exclusive frontier row stops new admission until every lane returns; the first spine row then admits alone ahead of ordinary work and remaining spine rows wait for later exclusive turns. Held rows drain and surface, and at a delegated tier dispatch one at a time, exclusive. The lane count resolves the command-line value, then the environment value, then the declared setting, then one; an absent, malformed or below-one value falls to serial. The empty-frontier census names unverified in-scope requirements, orphan rows and draft needs mechanically and hands them to the intake mint rather than minting in a lane.\"\"\"\r\n rationale = \"\"\"The §A4.1 authority flip: admission replaced the claim rung's deleted safety_class refusal, so the policy must live at ONE decision point and be driven as a pure function.\"\"\"\r\n@@\r\n code_symbol = \"_admit_parked/_stop_run/ensure_worktree/worker_argv/spawn_worker/run_worker/spawn_refresh\"\r\n-detail = \"\"\"One lane's mechanics ensure its worktree, hand the worker a single-item assignment, launch the worker and refresh subprocesses, and report outcomes without deciding them. A parked-lane resume refuses an assignment other than one item before mutation or launch; the tree signal is the one assigned specification leaving the claim directory, with exit codes as the remaining protocol.\"\"\"\r\n+detail = \"\"\"One lane ensures its worktree, forwards the launch session dials to its worker, hands that worker one item, and runs the station refresh as the lane�s own overlapping subprocess so lane bars do not queue at admission. It reports outcomes but decides none: the assigned specification leaving the claim directory and the exit code are the protocol. A parked resume refuses an assignment other than one item before mutation or launch.\"\"\"\r\n rationale = \"\"\"The §A4.2 split keeps the deciding half (dispatch.py) apart from the running half, so at lanes=1 the dispatcher degenerates to the serial loop and the concurrency is a table size, not a second code path.\"\"\"\r\n@@\r\n code_symbol = \"_dispatch_lock/claim/_claim_input_refusal/_claim_refusal/_abandoned_claim;commit\"\r\n-detail = \"\"\"The claim owns its dispatch-lock discipline and its bookkeeping commit. One claim commit moves one queued specification and cuts its branch; empty or multi-item input refuses before any move, commit, branch or worktree. Historical multi-item claim commits remain readable and are neither split nor re-claimed. The integration restriction retains its existing one-branch refresh behavior.\"\"\"\r\n+detail = \"\"\"The claim requires the dispatch lock, taken at one site after the refusal ladder so the lock does not create a refusal of its own. A hand claim on an idle station works; a hand claim during live lanes is unrepresentable; a lock-held caller proceeds without taking it again. One claim commit moves one queued specification and cuts its branch. Empty or multi-item input refuses before lock, move, commit, branch or worktree. Historical multi-item claim commits remain readable and are neither split nor re-claimed; each branch refresh remains independently restricted.\"\"\"\r\n rationale = \"\"\"A constraint instead of a check: the state the old refusal guarded against is unrepresentable, and separate exclusive turns preserve independent re-attestation windows for independent spine changes.\"\"\"\r\n@@\r\n code_symbol = \"SAFETY_CLASSES/_KIND_CONCURRENCY/_KIND_RANK/_lane_bar_directives\"\r\n-detail = \"\"\"The adjudication kind remains exclusive at rank 1. A lane whose one claimed row is adjudication runs no product bar; a lane whose one row is any other kind, or whose frontmatter is unreadable, runs the bar. The declared bar key sets that row's verification strictness without affecting scheduling, and a malformed value refuses before refresh.\"\"\"\r\n+detail = \"\"\"The adjudication kind is exclusive at rank one. Its lane runs no product bar because its outputs are status cells and the work registry; its refresh still incorporates trunk, runs the trunk step, and commits a verified no-bar attestation. A lane whose one claimed row is any other kind, or whose frontmatter is unreadable, runs the bar. The declared bar key states verification strictness without affecting scheduling; the refresh forwards that one row�s key to the gate check, absent k
[... byte cap hit — full stream in out/run-logs/ ...]
use a lane produces them in that order. The refusals, and every one of them is driven with the OTHER clauses satisfied, so each is the single thing that turns its commit away. A close carrying a HAND-WRITTEN subject is an ordinary work commit and does not peel; a commit with the PUBLIC mechanical prefix/suffix but a FORGED middle is refused because the attestor derives the actual active/ -> complete/ WI ids from the no-renames git diff and re-composes their exact canonical subject; a close carrying the machinery's own subject that also touched a path OUTSIDE docs/work/ does not peel either; and INSIDE docs/work/ is not enough, because only the move itself may create or destroy - a close that SMUGGLED a brand-new spec in beside the move, and a close that DESTROYED an already-terminal archived record beside it, are each refused, since peeling either would measure a spec's injection or a judged row's deletion at the parent where no reviewer ever saw it. A close whose pairs came out of a SECOND lane's active/ directory is refused by the one-source-branch requirement, driven with everything else valid - paths confined, deletions paired with their own additions, the subject exactly the one the writer composes for those ids - so nothing but that clause can be answering. THE MULTI-ROW SHAPE is driven too: a mechanical close moving two rows does not peel, failing toward more review. All the refusal arms are asserted to leave the gate refusing BY NAME on the round no longer naming the current tree, which is the fail-toward-MORE-review direction every unverified identity-moving step here takes. THE WRITER IS DRIVEN AGAINST THE VERIFIER, not only against fixtures the test file composes itself: a REAL close is landed through handback.close_adjudication and the commit it produces is asserted to peel back to exactly the rev the lane was on, so an ordering or a spelling that drifted on either side is a red rather than a silently un-peelable close on every adjudication lane. THE EMPTY CLOSE is driven where it is OBSERVABLE and its consequence is stated rather than assumed to match the others: a commit carrying the composed subject and a single parent that changed NOTHING - a real --allow-empty commit, since a zero-path diff is the one close shape a fixture cannot reach by writing files - is asserted refused AT mechanical_close_attestation, and deliberately NOT asserted at the gate, because measurement says the gate cannot see this refusal at all. Its refusal is OVER-DETERMINED and no clause owns it, which is stated rather than glossed: the one-source-branch requirement turns it away first, and with THAT deleted the empty diff derives no ids at all, whose composed subject (`adjudicate:  -> complete/ (mechanical close)`) cannot equal the one the commit carries - so the exact-subject comparison refuses it regardless, and there is deliberately no third non-emptiness clause, which could only ever fire where these two already had. The consequence is asserted beside the refusal because they are the honest pair: an empty commit preserves the identity by construction, so governing_rev's walk-through step reaches the real close underneath either way, and a test asserting a gate refusal here would be asserting a behaviour the module does not have and should not, since a commit that changed nothing has invalidated no verdict. THE TWO PEELS' REFUSAL ARMS are held by tests/test_integrate_station.py, cited beside this module because integrate re-exports these very functions (refresh_attestation, work_tip) and the station suite is where a refresh can be produced rather than hand-written: a genuine refresh attested to the sha it produced; a forged Bar-Green trailer in three shapes, the sharpest being a genuine refresh message copied verbatim onto another commit; an amend that keeps the message while the tree moves, revoking the attestation; the deliberately forged attestation recorded as a STATED limit rather than a defence; and the reset peel's data-loss half - an honest work commit merely QUOTING the trailer is never peeled away, and a genuine refresh above it peels back to exactly that commit. BOTH carriers are driven, not only the convenient one: that non-empty telemetry commit, and then the EMPTY commit agent_common.commit_telemetry writes when a Review-Verdict attestation must land on unchanged bookkeeping - obtained by CALLING that producer rather than by hand, so the two cannot drift apart, and asserted to really be zero-path, because that is the commit shape a walk classifying PATHS could not classify and so stopped at, burying the refresh under the very commit that recorded the approval. A WORK commit above the refresh does re-owe and does refuse, so the walk is proven to step through what cannot invalidate a verdict rather than through everything. BOTH ORDERS of refresh and round, because only one of them was covered and the other was broken: the round drawn AFTER the refresh - the order the shipped path actually produces, since a lane's refresh is spawned as soon as its worker is DONE and before the merge slot runs, so any slot refusal parks a branch with a refresh and no round - cites the POST-refresh sha, asserted in the fixture to be that sha and not the pre-refresh one, and is asserted to serve the lane at both readers and to carry the coordinator's attestation under the key the cross-check looks it up by, while a rework above it still re-owes. THE ATTESTATION'S CARRIER IS SCOPED TO ITS OWN PATHS, on BOTH arms and not only the one that carries a pathspec: with an unrelated work file staged and the bookkeeping unchanged, the commit agent_common.commit_telemetry writes for NAMED paths and the one it writes for NO paths at all - the call this suite itself makes, and the arm where a scope appended only when paths exist evaporates - are each asserted zero-path with the caller's index left exactly as found, so work cannot land under a bookkeeping label nor an attestation ride a commit that changed the tree. THE DIAL: the three values over a brief-and-drafts matrix, an unrecognized value falling to when-minting rather than to never, and an adjudication lane closing with a successor draft merging with no verdict artifact of any kind under both never and when-minting, while a spine draft still owes its round. THE DIAL AT THE SCHEDULER, the half a reader could otherwise only take on trust: a committing ADJUDICATE session is driven through the loop's own bookkeeping arm on a closed-lane repository at every dial value - including the `always` no repository fixture had reached - and the review queue it leaves is asserted together with the train-scoped diff range and the recorded judging family, which is what \"exactly as a committing BUILD does\" has to mean. Its INPUT is driven beside it: a branch carrying its spec in BOTH homes, the terminal copy drafting a spine successor and a stale active copy an ordinary one, is asserted to answer the scheduler and the merge gate the SAME way, with the shared precedence also driven pure on a two-path list and on the empty one. THE SHARED DEFINITION, in BOTH its dimensions. WHICH TREE: the C2 review-owed derivation answers owed after a rework and served after a fresh round, and record-only commits after the verdict re-owe nothing. HOW MANY PHASES: at a declared policy of 2 a lone logged REVIEW-A APPROVE is REFUSED by name and the gate clears only once a governing REVIEW-B joins it at the same identity; and the half-drawn round a killed run leaves - REVIEW-A served, the in-memory phase queue gone - is answered by both readers together, the derivation naming REVIEW-B and ONLY REVIEW-B while the gate refuses, then both agreeing once it lands, with the same fixture asserted SERVED at policy 1 so the answer is proven to come from the declared count. The phase span is driven pure at the values neither caller reaches - a negative policy, which a bare slice would answer by slicing from the END, and an over-dialled one - and an unparseable or refusable round is owed on both sides: it is drawn again and never clears the gate. The one class the readers still disagree on is a dissent: it is served for `phases_owed` and refused by the gate. THE TIER IS THE WHOLE CITED SET'S, not the majority's: the cited set includes slow modules, including test_integrate_admission, test_integrate_station, test_handback, test_bar_attestation and test_verdict_record, so Full is the cheapest tier at which EVERY arm above actually runs and Smoke would have claimed commit-floor coverage for a set the commit floor only partly runs. Tier and the pytest marker remain independent declarations that no check compares (registry-machinery-reference §12.2); this cell is labelled on the side that under-claims. THE GATING-SCOPE AND FILING BOUNDARY: a coordinator-recorded final claim-base round clears only with persisted-final-reviewer mode and reviewer retention on; retained-session full rounds and narrow rounds hold; a missing claim base holds by name; the full claim-base range survives a trunk refresh while a partial range cannot gate; a partial or refusable latest round holds without falling back to an older APPROVE and is owed again; neither a narrow approve nor an invalid round suppresses the unchanged-rework page; and a legacy rollup never clears. THE BAR ATTESTATION: a trailer validates only when its column-0 single label has its own tree and first parent, a known bar, and a tests digest; wrong tree or parent, missing or unknown bar, missing tests, a quoted or duplicate label refuse. Digesting normalizes and de-duplicates named paths, is order-independent, differs for a changed set, and gives none for an empty set. A verified review attestation is never recognized as a refresh by work_tip or governing_rev, while the read-only walk still steps through an identity-preserving review carrier; verified landing and no-bar refresh attestations still peel. The refresh writes landing or no-bar through the shared producer, and refresh and attest both reach that producer.\"\"\"\r\n+method = \"\"\"Drive verdict identity, evidence, phase, scope and attestation behavior beside their refusal cases. A mechanical close is admitted only for one moved row under the work registry with its scalar subject; empty and multi-row shapes do not peel and therefore fail toward more review. A real close and the verifier agree on that identity, while malformed subjects, outside paths, injected or destroyed records, invalid evidence, and unavailable repository answers retain their stated refusals.\"\"\"\r\n tier = \"Full\"\r\n*** End Patch\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
