{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"agent_message","text":"Completed the requested checkpoint text restoration. All edits are limited to the spine registries and retain LF.\n\n- LLR-061 `detail`\n  - Restored: explicit assignment context, prompt contents, generated-status exclusion, session tagging, evidence, branch-write limits, and trailer result channel.\n  - Replaced: multi-row prompt behavior with one-item refusal before session start.\n  - Deliberately retired: multi-row prompt block and track machinery.\n\n- LLR-144 `detail`\n  - Restored: immutable unique report, terminal move anti-livelock, quarantine, bar-inert patch, record-wise rename handling, checked command outcomes, restore-on-failed-revert, and finished outcomes.\n  - Replaced: several claimed specs/reports with one-spec close and one-report restoration.\n\n- LLR-149 `detail`\n  - Restored: approval-table behavior, held-row surface/drain behavior, exclusive barrier, lane-count ladder, and empty-frontier gap census.\n  - Replaced: simultaneous spine admission with first spine row alone and later rows waiting.\n\n- LLR-150 `detail`\n  - Restored: worktree, forwarded session dials, worker launch, refresh subprocess overlap, outcome-only role, tree/exit protocol.\n  - Replaced: list assignment with one item; parked list resumes now refuse before mutation or launch.\n\n- LLR-151 `detail`\n  - Restored: one-site dispatch lock, idle hand claim, live-lane hand claim unrepresentable, lock-held caller proceeds, bookkeeping commit, independent refresh restriction.\n  - Replaced: batch claim with one-spec claim; empty/multi-item input refuses before lock or state change.\n  - Preserved: historical joined claim records remain readable only.\n\n- LLR-152 `detail`\n  - Restored: exclusive rank, no-bar rationale, trunk incorporation, trunk step, verified no-bar attestation, bar-key forwarding, absent-key behavior, malformed refusal.\n  - Replaced only: mixed-batch arm with “a lane whose one row is any other kind runs the bar.”\n\n- LLR-161 `detail`\n  - Restored: report-first ordering, loud missing-report refusal, re-sweep behavior, genuinely second report/row, declared-rate complete-close spot check, successor lineage, and adoption sentence.\n  - Replaced: multi-report restoration with restoration of the one report created.\n\n- LLR-207 `detail`\n  - Restored: identity/evidence/attestation/phase/scope fail-closed contract and identity-preserving traversal.\n  - Replaced: multi-row/canonical-order explanation with one-row cardinality: empty and multi-row shapes decline to peel; one deletion implies one source branch; subject is scalar.\n  - Deliberately retired: empty-id-list and separate one-source-branch explanation.\n\n- TC-061 `method`, `evidence`\n  - Restored: worker prompt, result, relaunch, blocked, budget, review, concurrent-worker, managed-review, and preflight coverage.\n  - Replaced: two-row/walk claims with one-row completion read: committed trailer plus open specification is built but not done.\n  - Evidence preserves `tests/test_agent_loop_worker.py` and adds the refusal, prompt, and explicit-empty dispatch nodes.\n\n- TC-138 `method`, `evidence`\n  - Restored: one-spec close, report, terminal state, validator, second-close, loud missing-report, no-blockref, deliverable, no-claim, and all quarantine assertions.\n  - Replaced: multi-spec success with empty/multi-spec pre-state-change refusal.\n  - Evidence preserves module-level handback coverage and adds both new close-refusal nodes.\n\n- TC-143 `method`\n  - Restored: barrier behavior, approval table, lane-count ladder, gap census, and classification agreement.\n  - Replaced: batch spine admission with one-at-a-time spine admission.\n\n- TC-144 `method`\n  - Restored: needs-human handback, refresh subprocess, red-refresh quarantine, attended gate, census/intake, pause, dirty-tree, stall, and crash-resume assertions.\n  - Replaced: one spine batch/dual worker IDs with one-item claims and resumed one-item lane behavior.\n\n- TC-145 `method`\n  - Restored: dispatch-lock refusal, lock-held proceed, abandoned-claim re-cut, relink, minted-id, bookkeeping audit, and scratch-worktree isolation/cleanup/concurrent-drift arms.\n  - Replaced: batch claim with one-item claim and cardinality refusal.\n\n- TC-146 `method`\n  - Restored: rank, verified no-bar attestation, declared-bar forwarding, absent-bar no-gate arm, and malformed-value refusal.\n  - Replaced only: mixed-batch bar arm with any-other-kind one-row bar arm.\n\n- TC-154 `method`, `evidence`\n  - Restored: stable partition, held-stop, completion and census assertions.\n  - Replaced: ready spine batch with ready spine work item.\n  - Evidence preserves module-level loop-order evidence and adds the renamed node.\n\n- TC-156 `method`, `evidence`\n  - Restored: real trajectory check, loud missing report, second-close refusal, disposition, re-sweep, drafting, and adoption coverage.\n  - Replaced: multi-report restoration with restoration of the one report after injected failure.\n  - Evidence preserves handback/intake modules and adds the restoration node.\n\n- TC-205 `method`, `evidence`\n  - Restored: identity, evidence, phase, scope, attestation, real-close/verifier agreement, malformed subject/path/record/evidence refusals, and fail-closed unavailable answers.\n  - Replaced: canonical two-row peeling with scalar one-row admission; empty and multi-row closes do not peel.\n  - Evidence preserves verdict-record and real-close coverage and adds both two-row non-peel nodes.\n\nNo base obligation was intentionally omitted except:\n- batch/list/several-row/canonical-multirow clauses explicitly retired by the spec;\n- LLR-061’s retired track and multi-row prompt block;\n- LLR-207/TC-205’s obsolete empty-list-subject and independent source-branch explanation.\n\nI did not run lints, pytest, or a long ruling-5 scan, per the final instruction."}}
